## NVST_R_BUSY / "Failed to send custom app message" Warnings

These WebRTC warnings appear when Kit dispatches outbound events faster than the NVST data channel can deliver. Common triggers: high-frequency dispatches during WebRTC setup/teardown, client disconnect/reconnect, data channel saturation.

These are **cosmetic noise**, not errors. Messages are dropped on that frame and re-sent on the next successful tick. No action required unless warnings persist continuously (indicating the stream never connected).
